.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt HDIUTIL 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm hdiutil
.Nd manipulate disk images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm create
.Op Fl size Ar size
.Op Fl fs Ar filesystem
.Op Fl volname Ar name
.Op Fl layout Cm GPTSPUD | NONE
.Op Fl srcfolder Ar folder
.Op Fl ov
.Ar image
.Nm
.Cm attach
.Op Fl readonly
.Op Fl nomount
.Op Fl mountpoint Ar path
.Ar image
.Nm
.Cm detach | eject
.Op Fl force
.Ar device | mountpoint
.Nm
.Cm info
.Nm
.Cm imageinfo
.Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches disk images as disks through the kernel's MinkarDiskImage driver:
an image becomes
.Pa /dev/disk Ns Ar N ,
its partitions are published as on any disk, and their volumes are mounted
in
.Pa /Volumes
under their names.
It needs root.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm create
Make a raw image of
.Ar size
(with a
.Li b
(512-byte sectors),
.Li k , m , g
or
.Li t
suffix; or, with
.Fl srcfolder ,
large enough for the folder, whose contents are copied in).
The name gets
.Pa .dmg
unless it has an extension.
.Fl layout Cm GPTSPUD ,
the default, gives it a GUID partition table with one partition;
.Cm NONE ,
none.
.Fl fs
is
.Li HFS+
(the default),
.Li Journaled HFS+
or
.Li MS-DOS .
.Fl type
and
.Fl format
are accepted: the image is raw whatever they say.
.It Cm attach
Attach an image and mount its volumes
.Pf ( Fl nomount :
none;
.Fl mountpoint :
the first at
.Ar path ) .
A read-only image file, or
.Fl readonly ,
attaches read-only.
Prints the disk and its partitions, with their content and mount points.
.It Cm detach , eject
Unmount the image's volumes (by force with
.Fl force )
and detach it.
.It Cm info
List the attached images.
.It Cm imageinfo
Show an image's format and size.
.El
.Pp
Raw images (what
.Cm create
makes, and CD/DVD masters) and UDIF read/write images (UDRW) are read;
compressed and segmented UDIF images are not yet.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstyp 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_hfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
